-- title:
--   Regularity at a cusp from a power series chart
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain), let $\Lambda$ be a domain that is an $A$-algebra with injective structure map, and let $B$ be a Noetherian integrally closed domain that is an $A$-algebra. Suppose given ring homomorphisms $\iota : B \to \Lambda[[X]]$ and $\chi : B \to A$ such that $\chi$ reads off constant terms, in the sense that the image of $\chi(b)$ in $\Lambda$ equals the constant coefficient of $\iota(b)$ for all $b \in B$, and such that $\iota$ sends the image in $B$ of $a \in A$ to the constant power series attached to the image of $a$ in $\Lambda$. Suppose further given $u \in B$ with $\iota(u) = X w$ for some unit $w$ of $\Lambda[[X]]$, and a prime ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $B$ characterised by $b \in \mathfrak n \iff \chi(b) \in \mathfrak m_A$, and assume that every minimal prime $P$ of the principal ideal $(u)$ with $P \subseteq \mathfrak n$ equals $\ker \chi$. Let $\varpi \in A$ be irreducible, and let $B_{\mathfrak n}$ be any localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak n$. Then $B_{\mathfrak n}$ is a regular local ring, its Krull dimension is $2$, and the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak n$ in $B_{\mathfrak n}$ is generated by the images of $\varpi$ and $u$.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of the statement that a normal arithmetic surface carrying a power series chart (a $q$-expansion map) in which the chart parameter $u$ maps to $X$ times a unit is regular of dimension two at the point where that chart's cusp meets the special fibre, the hypothesis on minimal primes of $(u)$ expressing that no other cusp reduces to the same point. It is used in the analysis of the modular curve of full level at the cusp $\infty$, in particular by the regularity statements for the chart at that cusp.
